.nh
.TH "PB-DOMAIN-REMOVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-domain-remove - Remove a domain no tunnel or preview uses


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb domain remove <domain> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a domain from the workspace. A domain that a tunnel or preview still uses is refused,
and the message names the hostnames to remove first (pb tunnel domain remove). DNS records at
your provider are not touched; delete them there.

.PP
Confirmation is two steps. Run the command without --confirm: it changes nothing, shows what
would happen and prints a six-character code (exit status 2). Run the same command again with
--confirm CODE within 5 minutes. The code works once and only for that exact command and target.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code from the preview

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb domain remove dev.example.com
  pb domain remove dev.example.com --confirm A1B2C3
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-domain(1)\fP
